{
  "version": 1,
  "$comment": "Parts manifest. Each part is a GLB skinned to the base skeleton (bound by bone name at runtime). 'rig' limits a part to bases with that rig id (see src/config/bodies.json). Entries with rig 'figura_placeholder' are regenerated by scripts/gen-placeholders.mjs. See docs/parts.md. 'bodies' limits a part to those body ids (the v3.3 / v3.2 garments are anime-only, hair per sex); 'mobileFiles' maps a file to its .mobile.glb for touch devices; 'filesFor' pins files per animeBase (v3.8.2 defaults (v2.5; Blender Man's staging_v3.8.2 (v3.8 plus a rounder crown): every garment rebound to the v3.8 rest pose (arms lowered, legs in), pants knee keys re-transferred from the re-sculpted v3.8.2 body keys, female shorts front hem loosened 4 mm; v2.4 shipped v3.7.3 with the shirt push at body vert 2548, v2.3 v3.7.2): shirt / shorts / pants / sneakers are Blender Man's v3.7.x refits on both bodies (knee_bend_l / knee_bend_r keys on shorts (all zero) and pants, female shirt armpit push, female pants front hem back to the v3.7 shape) and all six hair styles are Blender Man's v3.8.2 refits to the shaved crown (long hair pushed out from the v3.7 head / ears; v3.6 to v3.3 pin the v3.3 hair); v3.6 and v3.6.nonmap pin the v3.6 refits; v3.5 and v3.4 pin the v1.9 set) (default files are v3.3; v3.2 keeps the v3.2 set; v3.1 / v3 / v2_eyetest keep v3.2 hair and bottoms with the v3 / old shirt and v3 cape). Real files are copied from figura-assets by scripts/sync-parts.mjs (manifest-additions.json is not used). Keys '<animeBase>+<preview>' in filesFor apply only with ?preview=<preview> (v3.6+f36r4: Blender Man's not-ready female shirt r4f / shorts r4p, desktop files only).",
